# Monthly Consistency vs Improvement
This chart shows how training consistency within each month relates to changes in aerobic efficiency over time.

Consistency (CV) measures how variable your runs are during a month. Lower values mean more stable training, while higher values indicate more variability.

The vertical axis shows the percentage change in aerobic efficiency compared to the previous month. Positive values indicate improvement, while negative values indicate decline.

This relationship is correlational and should be interpreted alongside training load, terrain, and intensity distribution.